{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Calibri;}}\fs22 Secure Your Account with Google Authenticator\line \line For your security, we require all users to enable Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) using the Google Authenticator app. This will serve as your security key for accessing your bank account.\line \line Step-by-Step Instructions:\line \line -\line Download Google Authenticator\line Install the app from the App Store (iOS) or Google Play Store (Android).\line \line -\line Enable 2FA in the Bank Portal\line \line -\line Log in to your online banking account.\line \line -\line Click on the More link in the top menu.\line \line -\line Select 2FA from the dropdown.\line \line -\line Follow the prompt to connect the Authenticator app.\line \line -\line Set Up the Authenticator App\line \line -\line Open the Google Authenticator app.\line \line -\line Tap the + icon in the lower right corner.\line \line -\line Select Scan a QR code.\line \line -\line Use your phone to scan the QR code displayed on the bank portal.\line \line -\line Enter the Code\line \line -\line Once scanned, the app will generate a 6-digit code.\line \line -\line Enter this code in the appropriate box on the website.\line \line -\line Save your settings and close your browser.\line \line In the future, each time you log in, youll be prompted to open the Authenticator app and enter your verification code, ensuring only you have access to your account.\line \line If you have any questions or need assistance, our support team is here to help.\line \line Thank you,\line US Capital Private Bank Client Relations}